    "description": "Generated from the current apps/api NestJS backend. Global prefix is `/api/v1` (except `health`, which is *supposed* to be excluded but isn't — see the note on the Health Check request). Two domains exist today: `health-check` and `example` (the generic CRUD reference template — real fields are literally `name`/`col1`/`col2`/`col3`).\n\nKnown bug (see CLAUDE.md): both `HealthCheckController` and `ExampleController` use bare `@Controller()` with argument-less `@Get()` handlers, so both resolve to `GET /api/v1`. Because `HealthCheckModule` is imported before `ExampleModule` in `app.module.ts`, the health check handler wins and `ExampleController.getAll` is currently unreachable through the HTTP layer.",
